      "id": "44c5b6fbfbe8-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "A circular coil having 'n' turns produces a field ______________ times larger than that produced by a single turn. 'n' &#2347;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2306;&#2337;&#2354;&#2368;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2375;&#2352;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; ______________ &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A circular coil having 'n' turns produces a field ______________ times larger than that produced by a single turn.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">'n' &#2347;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2306;&#2337;&#2354;&#2368;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2375;&#2352;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; ______________ &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "2n 2&#2319;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">2n</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2&#2319;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "n &#2319;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">n</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4n 4&#2319;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">4n</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4&#2319;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "3n 3&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">3n</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3&#2344;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>The magnetic field produced by a circular coil is directly proportional to the number of turns. If a coil has n turns, the field strength is n times that of a single-turn coil. This is because the field contributions from each turn add up constructively.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "44c5b6fbfbe8-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Which of the following statements is/are correct? Statements: 1) Ampere's Law describes the relationship between electric current and the magnetic field it produces. 2) Maxwell's equations are a set of four fundamental equations governing electric and magnetic fields in the absence of charges and currents. &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;/&#2361;&#2376;&#2306;? &#2325;&#2341;&#2344;: 1) &#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2368;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 2) &#2350;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2357;&#2375;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2380;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following statements is/are correct?</p><p>Statements:</p><p>1) Ampere's Law describes the relationship between electric current and the magnetic field it produces.</p><p>2) Maxwell's equations are a set of four fundamental equations governing electric and magnetic fields in the absence of charges and currents.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;/&#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p>&#2325;&#2341;&#2344;:</p><p>1) &#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2368;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>2) &#2350;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2357;&#2375;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2310;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2325;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2380;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Only Statement 2 &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 2",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Only Statement 2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Neither Statement 1 nor 2 &#2344; &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 1 &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; 2",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Neither Statement 1 nor 2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344; &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 1 &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; 2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Both Statements 1 and 2 &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 1 &#2324;&#2352; 2 &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Both Statements 1 and 2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 1 &#2324;&#2352; 2 &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Only Statement 1 &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 1",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Only Statement 1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; 1</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>&bull; Ampere's Law establishes a direct connection between electric currents and the magnetic fields they generate. This implies that the magnetic field in a region is influenced by the electric currents flowing in that region.</p><p>&bull; Maxwell's equations govern electric and magnetic fields in all scenarios, not just in the absence of charges and currents.</p><p>&bull; Maxwell's equations are four fundamental equations describing electric and magnetic fields:</p><p>&#9675; Gauss's Law for Electricity</p><p>&#9675; Gauss's law for Magnetism</p><p>&#9675; Faraday's Law of Induction</p><p>&#9675; Ampere-Maxwell Law</p>",
