      "number": 10,
      "question": "Which scientist suggested that the magnet must also exert an equal and opposite force on the current-carrying conductor? &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2376;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2361; &#2360;&#2369;&#2333;&#2366;&#2357; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2348;&#2354; &#2349;&#2368; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which scientist suggested that the magnet must also exert an equal and opposite force on the current-carrying conductor?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2376;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2361; &#2360;&#2369;&#2333;&#2366;&#2357; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2330;&#2369;&#2306;&#2348;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2348;&#2354; &#2349;&#2368; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Michael Faraday &#2350;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325;&#2354; &#2347;&#2376;&#2352;&#2366;&#2337;&#2375;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Michael Faraday</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325;&#2354; &#2347;&#2376;&#2352;&#2366;&#2337;&#2375;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Andre Marie Ampere &#2310;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2352;&#2368; &#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2368;&#2351;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Andre Marie Ampere</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2352;&#2368; &#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2368;&#2351;&#2352;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Joseph Henry &#2332;&#2379;&#2360;&#2375;&#2347; &#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Joseph Henry</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2379;&#2360;&#2375;&#2347; &#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352;&#2368;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "William Gilbert &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2327;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">William Gilbert</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2327;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>French scientist <b>Andre Marie Ampere (</b>1775 - 1836) suggested that the magnet must also exert an equal and opposite force on the current-carrying conductor.</p>",
